LINES
--------------

Here is some help for the test called lines.  

You can draw just one line with the pgm, or a circle-full of spokes.  You can
also control the number of spokes and whether the lines are erased or not.

Try the following:

  lines 10 200 200 100 1000 1
        ^   ^   ^   ^    ^  ^
        |   |   |   |    |  |
        |   |   |   |    |  +- test pattern #
        |   |   |   |    +- # of spokes
        |   |   |   +- length of line in pixels
        |   +---+ center (x,y)
        + iteration count (repeats entire test this number of times)

Here are some interesting things to try:

  lines 10 320 240 300 20 5     - concentric circles, draw/erase
  lines 10 200 200 100 1000 2   - sweeping line
  lines 2 100 100 50 7 6

The values for the test pattern are as follows:
    0 - draw 1 line (eg. lines <count> <x1> <y1> <x2> <y2>)
    1 - draw spokes from center to circumference
    2 - same as 1 but erase each line after we draw it
    3 - draw spokes from circumference to center
    4 - same as 3 but erase each line after we draw it
    5 - draw concentric circles (just the circumference)
    6 - draw shrinking spokes
    7 - draw rotating grid (busted)
    8 - draw rotating grid, one line per grid square
